ection fraud or foul play in 2020  which is of course an in defeasible  argument you can't  possibly argue against that if someone  is asserting that Michael Cohen said  he's worried that Donald Trump will not  relinquish control of the Oval Office if  indeed he loses in 2020 we've already  done a segment talking about how it's  unlikely in practice that it would  actually be allowed to happen by the  military and by law enforcement but all  of these ideas relate to ways that one  might hypothetically illegally seized  power or refused to relinquish it  Lawrence tribe brings us a different  idea the idea Lawrence tribe presented  on MSNBC over the weekend is that Donald  Trump we know he's willing to file to  declare bogus national emergencies over  things that are not actually emergencies  or crises the situation at the us-mexico  border being our example right now  Donald Trump Lawrence tribe suggests  would use a bogus national emergency  declaration to create a type of fear  that would maybe get him reelected in  November of 2020 that's the idea here is  Harvard Law Professor Lawrence tribe  saying it himself  we can't count on his being voted out of  office in 2020 he is sufficiently  corrupt and will probably have enough  help from not too friendly foreign  powers Russia Saudi Arabia  maybe Turkey so that we can't count on  removing this guy by an election and in  fact he may fabricate yet another  so-called national emergency to  influence that election what we have to  do is persistently gather the facts  right so what he is saying is not that  it would be an illegal seizure of the  White House or a refusal to accept the  results he's saying Trump could use  bogus national emergencies to get  reelected and of course in a country  where half the country doesn't vote half  the population doesn't vote and so many  people are voting based on incorrect  understandings of the world around them  it's not only plausible but it's  extraordinarily feasible to actually